    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d330">

                <pb facs="0401" n="1135" sameAs="frus:frus1895p2/pg1135"/>

                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Gresham to Baron Gresham.</hi>
                </head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Department of State</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1895-04-24"><hi rendition="#italic">April 24,
                        1895</hi>.</date></dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 52.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Excellency</hi>: I have the honor to acknowledge the
                    receipt of your note of February 26 last, stating that the cost of the surveys
                    ordered by the Samoan land commission aggregates perhaps $1,500 or $2,000, and
                    asking whether the Government of the United States is willing to pay its pro
                    rata share.</p>
                <p>In reply I have to inform you that this Government will bear its one-third share
                    of the expenses indicated, and that I have so advised the British ambassador in
                    reply to his recent note upon the subject.</p>
                <p>Accept, etc.,</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">W. Q. Gresham.</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
